    {
      "id": "claim_049cc06154054ddfbf73264e4b859520",
      "statement": "The three id-addressed portfolio routes each run `AuthorizationApi.check_entity_owned_by_user(user, portfolio)` in the router in addition to the service's own checks; that helper raises `HTTPException(404, \"Entity does not exist\")` for both a missing entity and one owned by another user, so a foreign portfolio is indistinguishable from an absent one and `test_portfolio_{update,delete,accounts_update}_not_owned` assert 404 exactly like their `*_not_found` siblings. `portfolio_accounts_sync` additionally repeats the account-ownership check at the router level before delegating, so no membership `DELETE` is issued until existence, portfolio ownership and account ownership have all passed.",
